# Testing Rules

## Purpose
Ensure changes are verified with tests that protect the architecture, contracts, and design-system boundary.

## Scope
All production code, generated code, and shared packages.

## Hard Constraints
- MUST add or update tests for any behavioral change.
- MUST test design-system components, backend services, DTO validation, and API contract changes.
- MUST keep tests deterministic and independent of network calls.
- MUST prefer focused unit tests plus contract tests over broad brittle snapshots.

## Best Practices
- SHOULD include at least one success path and one failure path for new logic.

## Enforceability
- Lint: flag test files that depend on real network or secrets.
- CI: run unit, integration, and contract test suites.
- Review: reject untested changes to routes, entities, or shared UI primitives.

## Examples
### ✅ Valid
```ts
expect(response.error).toBeNull();
```

### ❌ Invalid
```ts
await fetch('https://api.openai.com/v1/models');
```
